From e2b75ffe51da9aef1d7af1f7e15db0667eb7fff2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 21:32:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(teeth): Java and the shader were drawing different mouths
 from phase 4

GROUND_TRUTH.md D.1 makes the teeth the number-one priority fix. The build gate
ci/check_phase_uniform.py states the contract explicitly -- "the teeth are WHITE
at every storm phase; the aura is what changes colour" -- and enforces it on the
shaders. mcsm_teeth_color() returns vec3(1.0) for p >= 4.0, and mcsm_aura_color()
ramps 0.55/0.80/1.00 bluish -> pure white at 5.0 -> bluish 5.2 -> pure blue 6 ->
toxic green 7 -> blue 8.

McsmTeethPhaseTint said all of that in its header and then did the opposite in
its tables. PHASE_TRACK -- the teeth -- carried pink/purple at 4.2-5.5x, and
AURA_TRACK carried blue almost everywhere, including phase 7 where the shader
paints toxic green. Compared phase by phase the two implementations disagreed on
EVERY row:

  phase  shader teeth  java teeth        shader aura           java aura
  4      white         (1.00,0.45,0.85)  (0.55,0.80,1.00)      (0.25,0.50,1.00)
  5.0    white         (1.00,0.35,0.90)  (1.00,1.00,1.00) PURE (0.30,0.55,1.00)
  5.2    white         (0.85,0.40,1.00)  (0.50,0.78,1.00)      (0.22,0.48,1.00)
  6      white         (0.70,0.35,1.00)  (0.22,0.42,1.00)      (0.18,0.42,1.00)
  7      white         (0.90,0.30,0.95)  (0.36,1.00,0.28) GRN  (0.20,0.50,1.00)
  8      white         (0.80,0.40,1.00)  (0.35,0.58,1.00)      (0.25,0.55,1.00)

That is the "the mouths never matched the reference frames" symptom the header
claims to have fixed: a later "V2 revamp" moved the Java tables without moving
the shader, and the gate only ever inspected the shaders, so nothing caught it.
Java now takes its values from mcsm_teeth_color()/mcsm_aura_color() verbatim.
Three sources agree the teeth are white or cyan-white -- this file's own header,
GROUND_TRUTH.md B.1/E/G.3, and the enforced shader -- so the pink table was the
outlier.

Two further defects in the same file:

- glowStrength = Math.max(glowStrength, 4.5F) was a ONE-WAY RATCHET written
  straight into the player's persistent DabyWSClientConfig. Walk near one storm
  once and the bloom setting was 4.5 in every world forever, with nothing able to
  lower it. The other eight config fields the tick writes had no restore either,
  so a storm's last frame outlived the storm and became the player's "normal"
  colours.
  Now: the fields are snapshotted when the module takes over at phase 4 and handed
  back when the storm falls below it or the player leaves the world.

- `if (true) { ... }` around the beam colours: an unconditional block wearing a
  condition it never tested. Removed; the enclosing branch is already "the storm
  owns the mouth".

Intensity is deliberately NOT changed. GROUND_TRUTH.md G.3 asks for "~1.15 -- not
the old pure-white 2.4 blast" while check_phase_uniform.py pins a 4.0x floor and
the entity shader carries MCSM_MOUTH_GAIN = 4.0, citing a later brief. Those two
instructions contradict each other and nothing in the tree settles which
supersedes which, so the colours (provably wrong) are fixed and the brightness
(a judgement call) is flagged for the user rather than changed silently.

Gates: check_phase_uniform 520/520, palette_tables, shimcheck 174/174, preflight,
trace_sky_sheets, apply_stage_palette, sync_backdrop_palette, measure_stills,
iris_tu, content textures -- all pass. Aura verified numerically equal to the
shader at all five ramp stops.
